# Permissions the Android build is allowed to declare — SPEC-003 ADR-203, REQ-203.
#
# Checked against the **merged** manifest, not the one `tauri android init`
# writes. That one declares only INTERNET; Gradle merges each dependency's
# manifest at build time, and the merged result is what ships. A guard reading
# the post-init file would pass on every run and see none of this.
#
# One name per line. Blank lines and `#` comments ignored. A permission in the
# merged manifest and not on this list fails the build — so widening the app's
# access is a reviewed edit here, never a silent consequence of a dependency
# bump.
#
# Format: the bare name, without the `android.permission.` prefix.

# ── asked for, and understood ───────────────────────────────────────────────

# The app publishes signed deltas and resolves other people's identities.
INTERNET

# tauri-plugin-barcode-scanner — SCREEN-002's QR path. app.js branches on
# window.__TAURI__.barcodeScanner to choose scan-or-type; without this the
# scanner is absent and every link falls back to the typed code.
CAMERA

# tauri-plugin-biometric — REQ-024's user-presence check before any root-key
# use. USE_FINGERPRINT is the pre-API-28 spelling of the same capability.
USE_BIOMETRIC
USE_FINGERPRINT

# ── arrived from dependencies, not yet explained ────────────────────────────
#
# These are on the list because they are already in the merged manifest and the
# build must be able to pass. Being listed is NOT an endorsement — each is an
# open question in SPEC-003 OBS-202. They are written down here rather than
# excluded so the check can run at all, and grouped separately so nobody
# mistakes "passes CI" for "reviewed and wanted".

# Signature-level, for reading system service state. Nobody chose this, and the
# contributing library is still unidentified — two attempts at parsing Gradle's
# manifest-merger report failed. On a root-key custodian this is the line in
# this file most worth resolving. SPEC-003 OBS-202.
DUMP

# Almost certainly an AndroidX/WorkManager service declaration rather than a
# capability the app exercises. Confirm before treating as intended.
BIND_JOB_SERVICE

# Probably the biometric prompt's haptic feedback.
VIBRATE

# Probably a networking library checking connectivity before a request.
ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE
